<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hurricane Irma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2017</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hurricane Irma was a Category 5 Atlantic hurricane that struck the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> in September 2017, one of the strongest recorded in the open Atlantic. It destroyed most buildings on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbuda">Barbuda</a>, forcing the evacuation of the whole island, and devastated Sint Maarten and other islands before hitting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-irma.jpg" alt="Hurricane Irma" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NOAA's GOES 16 Satellite · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Irma_2017-09-06_1230Z.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
